eac3to-go
=========

Native media demuxing and audio processing in Go, with eac3to 4.00 behavior
as the compatibility reference. The project is under development. It is not
yet a complete replacement for every Windows eac3to operation.

  make build
  make decoder
  make windows
  make check

Use bin/eac3to --help for available options. Linux builds use native Cgo SSRC
and Aften processing. Windows builds use an isolated checksum-pinned MinGW
toolchain; see scripts/build-windows.py. Media probing and some codecs use
separate FFmpeg/FFprobe executables. Existing system installations and libFDK
support are never replaced by the build scripts.
Disc probing requires FFprobe with libbluray enabled. Keep the FFmpeg/FFprobe
pair together; explicit --ffmpeg and --ffprobe paths take priority.

  eac3to /disc/BDMV
  eac3to /disc/BDMV --main
  eac3to /disc/BDMV -demux -destpath=/output
  eac3to /disc/BDMV --playlist=00001 2: video.h264 3: audio.dts
  eac3to input.wav output.flac
  eac3to input.wav output.wav -25.000 -changeTo24.000 +100ms

Quote paths containing spaces and title selectors such as '1)' when using a
shell. Existing outputs require --force. Unsupported operations fail explicitly.
--allow-unverified enables comparison paths; it does not establish parity.

--report=/path/to/extraction.json writes a successful extraction manifest with
the final output paths and residual mux delays. It is intended for muxers that
need sample/frame-aligned extraction without dropping the remaining offset.
The report is published only after every requested output succeeds.

Playlist selection combines authored main-feature labels, navigation evidence,
clip metadata, picture-language branches and playlist families. Ambiguous discs
require --playlist. It does not claim universal Java/menu emulation.

Keep compressed sources in their original codec for stream extraction. Audio
conversion has codec-specific requirements; lossless output alone does not
make every decoder equivalent. The separate pinned decoder profile has a
bounded Windows comparison corpus. --reference-tail reproduces historical
resampler tail behavior; normal draining preserves the complete filter tail.

Tests use generated format fixtures and sample/byte comparisons. Full-disc
test media and local comparison records are not distributed with this source.
Third-party source retains its original licenses and attribution under
third_party; build scripts and patches are included for rebuilding it.
